Package: TriCopula
Type: Package
Title: Joint Maximum-Likelihood Trivariate Copula Regression
Version: 0.17.4
Authors@R: c(
    person("Ibrahim", "Niankara", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "Ibrahim.niankara@aaua.ac.ae"),
    person("BRASS Digital Lab", role = "fnd",
           comment = "LLC registered in Burkina Faso, RCCM BF-OUA-01-2026-B13-02466; https://brassbe1982-bdlweb.share.connect.posit.cloud/"))
Description: Full maximum-likelihood estimation of copula distributional
    regression models for three continuous responses. The margins are
    Gaussian, log-normal, Gamma, Weibull, inverse Gaussian, Beta, generalized
    Pareto, Dagum or Singh-Maddala, with a predictor for every parameter.
    Dependence is described by a trivariate Gaussian or Student-t copula, or
    by a C-vine pair-copula construction as in Aas, Czado, Frigessi and Bakken
    (2009) <doi:10.1016/j.insmatheco.2007.02.001> with Gaussian, Student-t,
    Clayton, Gumbel, Frank and Joe pair copulas and their rotations, whose
    parameters may depend on covariates as in the copula additive models of
    Marra and Radice (2017) <doi:10.1016/j.csda.2017.03.004>. All parameters
    are estimated jointly, with analytic gradients, observed-information and
    sandwich covariance matrices. Predictors may contain penalized smooth
    terms; the likelihood accommodates prior weights, responses missing at
    random, truncation and censoring. Functions for model selection and
    inference after selection, a test of the simplifying assumption, joint
    probabilities, marginal effects, diagnostics and simulation are provided.
